# nr-exthost-pdf-codec wiring (core): the new crate `mixdog-pdf-codec` (PDF stream filters and the standard security handler, ported from pdf.js 6.4.299).

The crate is in `native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf-codec` (Cargo.toml, NOTICE, src/, tests/vectors.rs). It has no protocol rows, no registration and
no SERVICE_PENDING entry: nothing in the daemon calls it yet (nr-exthost-pdf-document in wave 2 does).

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml

(a) `[workspace] members`: after `"crates/mixdog-exthost",` (or beside the other leaf crates) add

    "crates/mixdog-pdf-codec",

(b) `[workspace.dependencies]`, in the internal crates block after `mixdog-exthost = { path = "crates/mixdog-exthost" }`:

    mixdog-pdf-codec = { path = "crates/mixdog-pdf-codec" }

(c) `[workspace.dependencies]`, in the registry crates (alphabetical; `sha2 = "0.10"` and `unicode-normalization = "0.1"` are already there:
do not add them again, a duplicate key breaks the manifest). Both are already in Cargo.lock and in the local cargo cache at these versions
(aes 0.8.4, md-5 0.10.6); nothing new is downloaded:

    aes = "0.8"
    md-5 = "0.10"

`weezl` and `cbc` are not used: the LZW decoder is a port (weezl does not give pdf.js's output on a stream with no end-of-data code or on an EarlyChange
other than 0 and 1), and the AES-CBC chaining is a loop over the `aes` block cipher because pdf.js's framing (IV prefix, a partial block dropped per
call, padding removed only when it agrees with its count) is not what `cbc` does.

## 2. native/core/Cargo.lock

Add the package entry (cargo writes it; `--locked` needs it present):

    [[package]]
    name = "mixdog-pdf-codec"
    version = "1.5.0"
    dependencies = [
     "aes",
     "md-5 0.10.6",
     "mixdog-workspace-hack",
     "sha2 0.10.9",
     "unicode-normalization",
    ]

(`md-5` and `sha2` have two versions in the lock, so those two are written with their version.)

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

The crate depends on `mixdog-workspace-hack` like its siblings. Regenerate the hack (hakari) after (1) so the feature set of aes, md-5, sha2 and
unicode-normalization is the unified one; if hakari adds nothing, nothing changes.

## 4. mixdog-testkit tests/cfg_test_guard.rs

Nothing: the crate is not in `LIBRARIES` (no replays move out of it) and has no `cfg(test)` item besides `tests/vectors.rs`.

## 5. Verify (after 1 and 2)

    cargo nextest run -p mixdog-pdf-codec --offline
    cargo clippy -p mixdog-pdf-codec --all-targets --offline -- -D warnings
